        "passage": "Do you know how to keep healthy? Here are some tips for you.\n\nFirst, eat a balanced diet. You should eat more vegetables and fruits, but less junk food. Different kinds of food give you different nutrients.\n\nSecond, exercise regularly. You can run, swim, or play basketball. Exercise helps you stay strong and happy. Try to exercise at least 30 minutes every day.\n\nThird, get enough sleep. Most teenagers need 8-10 hours of sleep every night. Going to bed early and getting up early is a good habit.\n\nFinally, drink enough water. Water is very important for your body. You should drink at least 8 glasses of water every day.\n\nIf you follow these tips, you will be healthier and happier.\n\n---\n\nThe Internet has changed our lives in many ways. We can use it to learn, work, shop, and communicate with friends.\n\nHowever, the Internet also brings some problems. Some students spend too much time playing online games. This is bad for their eyes and studies. Some people share too much personal information online, which can be dangerous.\n\nTo use the Internet safely, you should follow these rules: First, don't spend more than two hours online each day. Second, never share your real name, address, or phone number with strangers. Third, if someone says something bad to you online, tell your parents or teachers immediately.\n\nThe Internet is a useful tool, but we must use it wisely. Remember, the Internet is a tool, not your whole life. Go outside, talk to real people, and enjoy the real world!",
