        "passage": "Spring Festival is the most important traditional festival in China. It usually comes in January or February. Before Spring Festival, people clean their houses, buy new clothes, and prepare delicious food.\n\nOn Spring Festival Eve, families get together and have a big dinner. The most popular food is dumplings. In some places, people also eat fish, because the Chinese word for 'fish' sounds like 'surplus'.\n\nAfter dinner, families watch the Spring Festival Gala on TV. At midnight, people set off fireworks to welcome the new year. Children are very happy because they can get red envelopes with money inside.\n\nDuring Spring Festival, people visit their relatives and friends. They say 'Happy New Year' to each other. It is a time for family, love, and hope for the future.\n\n---\n\nDo you know how to keep healthy? Here are some tips for you.\n\nFirst, eat a balanced diet. You should eat more vegetables and fruits, but less junk food. Different kinds of food give you different nutrients.\n\nSecond, exercise regularly. You can run, swim, or play basketball. Exercise helps you stay strong and happy. Try to exercise at least 30 minutes every day.\n\nThird, get enough sleep. Most teenagers need 8-10 hours of sleep every night. Going to bed early and getting up early is a good habit.\n\nFinally, drink enough water. Water is very important for your body. You should drink at least 8 glasses of water every day.\n\nIf you follow these tips, you will be healthier and happier.",
